      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For reasons I’m not going to go into great detail on this comment, VRChat Lite is impossible. That fattest part is the Unity engine, which should be scrapped even for the full version.\n\nThe second fattest part is the IK system, which MUST run on EVERY version of the game in which ANY person on screen has VR.\n\nThe third fattest part are overwhelming material/shader counts on unoptimized avatars.\n\nAs for 32-bit support, if you can’t get Windows in 64-bit, buy literally any new computer. Buy a Raspberry Pi 3 for $30. Even that tiny thing has 64-bit.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-07-28T12:28:58.697Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "the world needs a \"VR\"chat version for cheaper devices. I would see a boost in popularity since normal vrchat is widely promoted as a VR exlusive title. VRchat is NOT a vr-exlusive title, but still is a heavvy program, because it was designed for VR. VRchatLite would be targeted at low/end PCs(and make way for Android-Ios versions) and would have the VR optional. VRchat lite would be able to run on 32bit computers thanks to the VR part  not being in it. some feutures that would be turned of in VRchatLite should be avaible for download, because for example full body tracking could be used for monitor-only gameplay, but is not nessesery for nonVR use of the game. please consider my idea. Thanks! ~some guy who happens to have this concept",
